#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts: {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep kritis: {#critical-concepts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the measurement of a qubit in a superposition is probabilistic, like flipping a coin, the superposition state itself behaves differently than a flipping coin.\n"
msgstr "Meskipun pengukuran qubit dalam superposisi bersifat probabilistik, seperti melempar koin, keadaan superposisi itu sendiri berperilaku berbeda dari koin yang melayang.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A main difference between a classical probability distribution and a superposition is that the superposition has *phase* coherence, which allows it to interfere constructively or destructively.\n"
msgstr "Perbedaan utama antara distribusi probabilitas klasik dan superposisi adalah bahwa superposisi memiliki *koherensi fase*, yang memungkinkannya berinterferensi secara konstruktif atau destruktif.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The state of a single, isolated qubit can be visualized as a point on the so-called \"Bloch sphere,\" where the relative amplitudes of the $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ components determine the polar angle $\\theta$ and the relative phases between the two components determine the azimuthal angle $\\phi$.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan satu qubit terisolasi bisa divisualisasikan sebagai sebuah titik di atas yang disebut \"bola Bloch,\" di mana amplitudo relatif komponen $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ menentukan sudut polar $\\theta$ dan fase relatif antara kedua komponen menentukan sudut azimut $\\phi$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All single-qubit quantum gates can be viewed as rotations of the vector on this sphere.\n"
msgstr "Semua Gate kuantum satu qubit bisa dipandang sebagai rotasi vektor pada bola ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F questions: {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan B/S: {#tf-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F A quantum superposition is basically the same as a probabilistic event in classical physics, like flipping a coin.\n"
msgstr "B/S Superposisi kuantum pada dasarnya sama dengan kejadian probabilistik dalam fisika klasik, seperti melempar koin.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F The length of the Bloch vector describing the state of a single isolated qubit is always 1.\n"
msgstr "B/S Panjang vektor Bloch yang menggambarkan keadaan satu qubit terisolasi selalu 1.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "T/F Single-qubit quantum gates do not change the length of the Bloch vector.\n"
msgstr "B/S Gate kuantum satu qubit tidak mengubah panjang vektor Bloch.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "MC questions: {#mc-questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan pilihan ganda: {#mc-questions}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the correct Bloch vector that represents the state $|\\Psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}|0\\rangle + e^{i \\pi / 4} \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}|1\\rangle$ :\n"
msgstr "Pilih vektor Bloch yang tepat yang merepresentasikan keadaan $|\\Psi\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}|0\\rangle + e^{i \\pi / 4} \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}|1\\rangle$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Four Bloch spheres are shown. The vector points nearly along +x in option a, halfway between +x and +y and slightly below the xy plane in option b, between +x and -y, and slightly above the xy plane in option c, and along -x in option d. ](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/superposition-with-qiskit/mc-question.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Four Bloch spheres are shown. The vector points nearly along +x in option a, halfway between +x and +y and slightly below the xy plane in option b, between +x and -y, and slightly above the xy plane in option c, and along -x in option d. ](/learning/images/modules/quantum-mechanics/superposition-with-qiskit/mc-question.avif)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
